{"kind":"request","text":"The desktop AI app does not render a card: remove the sandbox domain it refuses\n\nScope: J2's acceptance, 2082efd9. Hugh ran the person's steps at about 11:07 EST. The server connected, and the app showed \"There was a problem displaying content from dap-views.\" instead of the card.\n\nWhat the log shows (`~/Library/Logs/Claude/mcp-server-dap-views.log`): `initialize`, `tools/list` and `resources/list` at 16:06, and `resources/read` id 4 at 16:07:02 with a result. It holds no `tools/call`, so this session signed nothing.\n\nThe likely cause, not yet proven: every view resource declares `_meta.ui.domain` as `\u003clabel\u003e.inguz.space`, from `sandboxDomain` in `packages/mcp/src/views/hosts.ts`. The MCP Apps specification says each host sets that field's format and rules. Claude's troubleshooting page says the value must be `{hash}.claudemcpcontent.com`, hashed from the connector URL, and that a bad value gets an error in place of the app. The specification says that when the field is omitted, the host uses its default sandbox origin. The 17 October prototypes `dap-cards`, `dap-cycle` and `dap-grow` declare no domain, and they rendered in this app. I read the app's message as this refusal, and I have not seen the app log that reason.\n\nSources: https://claude.com/docs/connectors/building/mcp-apps/troubleshooting.md and the specification at https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/ext-apps/blob/main/specification/2026-01-26/apps.mdx.\n\nDo this:\n1. Omit `_meta.ui.domain` unless a deployment declares a domain for a host that accepts it. The local stdio path has no connector URL to hash. Correct what notes/2026-10-17-compact-cards-design.md and any document say about `inguz.space` as the origin for these resources, since that holds for a dap web host and not for this app.\n2. Give the fix its own request and head, because 2082efd9 stays open. Add a test that the resource carries no domain by default, and a control.\n3. Say what a hosted view would need for this app, in one paragraph, and build nothing for it.\n4. Move the person's steps to the head that holds the fix, then tell me. Hugh runs them again. The other two unknowns of the app stay unknown until then.\n\nIf removing the domain is not the cause, the next run shows it. Before that run, read what else differs from `~/play/dap-views-prototype/cards-server.mjs`, such as the resource's `csp` and `permissions` as empty objects, and the 1 MiB bound against the bundle's size, and list the differences in your note, so a second failure has a next step.\n\nNo card from the landed view kit has rendered in this app, to my knowledge. Treat S2's desktop acceptance as open with this.\n\nOrder: first, ahead of J5's landing if it does not block J5's work.","body":{"conditions":"View resources carry no sandbox domain by default, under a test and a control, approved by the checker and landed on main, with the person's steps moved to that head.","target_head":"415fc26540de19541f174d5674fe691bd0c927e7","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}